translated_text:
VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF JOMBANG,
Considering: a. that in order to optimize efforts leading to the reduction of violence against women and children, it is deemed necessary to improve services for the protection of women and children victims of violence; b. that to achieve the purpose of consideration letter a, it is deemed necessary to regulate the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence by stipulating its provisions in a Regional Regulation.
In View of: 1. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3143);
2. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3668);
3. Law Number 23 of 1992 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1992 Number 100); 4. Law Number 20 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 138 concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);
5. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
6. Law Number 1 of 2000 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 182 concerning the Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labor (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);
7. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
8. Law Number 10 of 2004 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 53, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4389);
9. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
10. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437) as amended for the second time by Law Number 12 of 2008 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844); 11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence
12. Presidential Decree of the Republic of Indonesia Number 36 of 1990 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Rights of the Child;
13. Presidential Decree of the Republic of Indonesia Number 88 of 2002 concerning National Action Plan (RAN) for the Elimination of Trafficking in Women and Children;
14. Presidential Decree of the Republic of Indonesia Number 61 of 2003 concerning National Action Plan for Human Rights of Indonesia 1998-2003.
With Mutual Agreement

